1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.810
Hey everybody. Welcome to the podcast.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:07.090
Very excited because my guest today is Mary Cain,

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.120
the Mary Cain.

4
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.200
The track and field athlete who by high school

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.000
had established herself as the fastest girl in a generation.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.650
The Mary Cain who at 17

7
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.860
became the youngest American ever

8
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.720
to make a world championship track and field team.

9
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.070
The Mary Cain for whom

10
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.760
Olympic glory seemed a foregone conclusion,

11
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.330
until that is, she joined Nike's elite Oregon Project

12
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.360
under Alberto Salazar.

13
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.810
Within that culture, her body ultimately collapsed,

14
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.720
her running career behind it.

15
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.600
And for a couple of years thereafter,

16
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.470
she just kind of disappeared,

17
00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:51.470
until November of 2019 that is when Mary broke her silence

18
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.570
on what happened and why,

19
00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.180
telling her story by way of a video op-ed

20
00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.037
in "The New York Times" entitled,

21
00:00:59.037 --> 00:01:04.037
"I Was the Fastest Girl in America, Until I Joined Nike".

22
00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.230
That video went crazy viral.

23
00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:10.900
It resulted in a groundswell of global support for Mary,

24
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.290
and opened the door to a broader ongoing conversation

25
00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.050
around the toxicity that pervades female athletics,

26
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.650
and the means by which we can construct a better future

27
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.490
for women and girls in sports.

28
00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:28.690
Not content to merely tell her story

29
00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:32.600
or just get back to running, but to actually do something,

30
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.170
make a real difference,

31
00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.160
Mary just announced the launch of Atalanta,

32
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.820
a New York City based elite running team

33
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.880
and community nonprofit.

34
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.810
It's an endeavor that she leads as CEO,

35
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.900
with the dual mission of promoting running community,

36
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.410
inclusivity and diversity,

37
00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.960
and rewriting the rule book on

38
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.320
professional women's athletics.

39
00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.940
Today, we get into all of it.

40
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.480
Her story is powerful.

41
00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.340
This one is kind of a wild, emotional ride,

42
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.430
and I'm really proud to help share it.

43
