00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:41.444
and kind of the early days of working with Alberto

492
00:21:41.444 --> 00:21:43.260
at the Nike Oregon Project.

493
00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:47.563
Yeah, so I first met him the beginning of my junior year,

494
00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:49.580
and I still lived in New York,

495
00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:51.520
I was still a high school junior,

496
00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:54.710
and we had this long distance relationship,

497
00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:57.140
my junior and senior year,

498
00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:59.190
during which I ended up qualifying

499
00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:01.540
for the world championships at the end of my junior year,

500
00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:04.360
signing a professional contract with Nike

501
00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:07.520
my fall senior year,

502
00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:10.430
and then going on to have a really incredible

503
00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.798
senior year season.

504
00:22:11.798 --> 00:22:14.413
And he's coaching you remotely at that point.

505
00:22:14.413 --> 00:22:16.680
Yeah, and there are times where maybe

506
00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:21.300
we were at the same meet together, or I travel out to,

507
00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:25.220
like that summer that I competed on the world stage

