you're really trying to do something good in the world.

2507
01:56:40.290 --> 01:56:43.110
Let's support you."

2508
01:56:43.110 --> 01:56:45.947
If anything in the traditional space, it's much more like,

2509
01:56:45.947 --> 01:56:49.470
"No, you're not that fast anymore. Whatever."

2510
01:56:49.470 --> 01:56:51.980
Yeah, and everybody's running to protect their own

2511
01:56:51.980 --> 01:56:52.813
at the same time.

2512
01:56:52.813 --> 01:56:55.020
I mean, it is a David and Goliath story.

2513
01:56:55.020 --> 01:56:57.460
It's not just, "Hey, this is Mary Cain,

2514
01:56:57.460 --> 01:57:01.550
and she's gonna share her story of how hard it was."

2515
01:57:01.550 --> 01:57:06.470
This is you basically taking on Nike.

2516
01:57:06.470 --> 01:57:09.130
I mean, that's a very,

2517
01:57:09.130 --> 01:57:11.100
and you're a young person,

2518
01:57:11.100 --> 01:57:12.570
that's very scary,

2519
01:57:12.570 --> 01:57:15.110
and you still wanna have this career in running.

2520
01:57:15.110 --> 01:57:16.400
So you're gonna become,

2521
01:57:16.400 --> 01:57:18.980
you're risking becoming persona non grata in doing this.

2522
01:57:18.980 --> 01:57:23.980
And that takes an unbelievable amount of courage to do that.

2523
01:57:26.397 --> 01:57:28.020
And I thank you for saying that.

2524
01:57:28.020 --> 01:57:32.150
And I think again though the almost sad thing is that

2525
01:57:32.150 --> 01:57:34.950
yes, it was courageous, and yes, I was being vulnerable,

2526
01:57:36.100 --> 01:57:39.950
but that was pure fear that was guiding me.

2527
01:57:39.950 --> 01:57:41.620
And it wasn't fear of repercussions,

2528
01:57:41.620 --> 01:57:45.940
it wasn't fear of the big, bad guy,

2529
01:57:45.940 --> 01:57:49.163
it was fear that somebody was living a lie,

2530
01:57:49.997 --> 01:57:53.900
and hurting themselves because they didn't know it.

2531
01:57:53.900 --> 01:57:56.700
And it was fear for that younger version of myself.

2532
01:57:56.700 --> 01:57:58.720
It was that fear of that version of myself

2533
01:57:58.720 --> 01:58:02.350
from 72 hours before that drove me.

2534
01:58:02.350 --> 01:58:06.030
And I say that in so much as to say

2535
01:58:06.030 --> 01:58:10.030
I think these issues are terrifying.

2536
01:58:10.030 --> 01:58:15.030
I think the fact that we don't support and protect people,

2537
01:58:15.330 --> 01:58:20.330
and treat them as these incredible gifts,

2538
01:58:21.610 --> 01:58:25.520
and I say this in a very general way outside of sport way,

2539
01:58:25.520 --> 01:58:28.210
people are people they're not products.

2540
01:58:28.210 --> 01:58:31.770
And when organizations lose sight of that

2541
01:58:31.770 --> 01:58:36.510
and take advantage of people, that goes beyond sport.

2542
01:58:36.510 --> 01:58:39.950
Women being taken advantage of goes beyond sport.

2543
01:58:39.950 --> 01:58:42.400
Women being objectified, this is like,

2544
01:58:42.400 --> 01:58:44.890
the reason 17 million people watched it

2545
01:58:44.890 --> 01:58:46.867
is because it's not just a sport story,

2546
01:58:46.867 --> 01:58:49.300
and it's not even just a woman's story.

2547
01:58:49.300 --> 01:58:54.300
This is when powerful people abuse.

2548
01:58:56.300 --> 01:59:00.540
And what is power? It depends on the situation.

2549
01:59:00.540 --> 01:59:02.280
And so, there are plenty of people in the world

2550
01:59:02.280 --> 01:59:04.080
with power over others.

2551
01:59:04.080 --> 01:59:09.080
And the idea that somebody was trapped in that was,

2552
01:59:11.024 --> 01:59:13.133
that fear guided me.

2553
01:59:14.360 --> 01:59:16.980
And so, when people say I was brave or courageous,

2554
01:59:16.980 --> 01:59:19.420
I thank them, I appreciate that,

2555
01:59:19.420 --> 01:59:23.730
but this wasn't a moment for me.

2556
01:59:23.730 --> 01:59:28.040
This was literally me chucking the baton across the room,

2557
01:59:28.040 --> 01:59:29.670
and being like, "Save yourself"

