2811
02:10:44.100 --> 02:10:47.613
that I'm embarking on with a cynical perspective,

2812
02:10:48.510 --> 02:10:52.510
which I think would be really, really easy for me to do

2813
02:10:52.510 --> 02:10:53.850
if I'm honest.

2814
02:10:53.850 --> 02:10:57.362
And so, there's so much importance to me-

2815
02:10:57.362 --> 02:10:59.464
To fuck all those Nice guys team.

2816
02:10:59.464 --> 02:11:00.297
Yeah, exactly.

2817
02:11:00.297 --> 02:11:02.653
That's the name of the team.
Pretty much.

2818
02:11:03.590 --> 02:11:06.910
It's really important for me to think about

2819
02:11:08.830 --> 02:11:12.190
so many people who've helped me,

2820
02:11:12.190 --> 02:11:15.090
and so many people who supported me through that time,

2821
02:11:15.090 --> 02:11:16.610
like the Alexis,

2822
02:11:16.610 --> 02:11:20.140
or people who just, like the Wess,

2823
02:11:20.140 --> 02:11:23.570
who stepped up and said like, "I'm here for you."

2824
02:11:23.570 --> 02:11:26.460
Because those are the people who I can lean on

2825
02:11:26.460 --> 02:11:29.650
and learn from when creating something beautiful,

2826
02:11:29.650 --> 02:11:31.890
versus just kind of creating something

2827
02:11:31.890 --> 02:11:35.090
out of a fear of what was.

2828
02:11:35.090 --> 02:11:39.127
When you look on the past, it can't ever be like

2829
02:11:39.127 --> 02:11:42.280
I'm just trying to rewrite my own story.

2830
02:11:42.280 --> 02:11:46.123
It's how can I really make something good going forward?

2831
02:11:47.120 --> 02:11:49.160
And so that's why I do think,

2832
02:11:49.160 --> 02:11:52.040
although obviously I've cried multiple times,

2833
02:11:52.040 --> 02:11:54.010
it's healthy to talk about,

2834
02:11:54.010 --> 02:11:56.410
and it's important to talk about,

2835
02:11:56.410 --> 02:11:59.190
especially when I just held this in for so long.

2836
02:11:59.190 --> 02:12:01.030
And you still look back on that

2837
02:12:02.130 --> 02:12:06.190
moment of me running out into the thunderstorm,

2838
02:12:06.190 --> 02:12:10.120
which is so dramatic but literally what happened,

2839
02:12:10.120 --> 02:12:15.120
as being this almost example of how weak I was.

2840
02:12:16.740 --> 02:12:18.680
And that was the narrative.

2841
02:12:18.680 --> 02:12:21.280
The narrative was in my head

2842
02:12:21.280 --> 02:12:24.770
because this is what was told to me, "You're a head case.

2843
02:12:24.770 --> 02:12:26.340
This is due our fault.

2844
02:12:26.340 --> 02:12:28.700
You're the one failing yourself."

2845
02:12:28.700 --> 02:12:33.310
And for so long that's how I kind of remembered it.

2846
02:12:33.310 --> 02:12:37.150
And to suddenly take a step back and look at it

2847
02:12:37.150 --> 02:12:40.810
almost from the eyes of everybody but me,

2848
02:12:40.810 --> 02:12:44.860
it suddenly, wow, that's horrible that that happened,

2849
02:12:44.860 --> 02:12:48.170
and how can I make sure it never does again?

2850
02:12:48.170 --> 02:12:49.520
Yeah.

2851
02:12:49.520 --> 02:12:50.960
It also wasn't that long ago.

2852
02:12:50.960 --> 02:12:52.240
I mean, the pandemic,

2853
02:12:52.240 --> 02:12:55.820
anything pre-pandemic feels like 100 years ago,

2854
02:12:55.820 --> 02:12:58.410
but we're talking about the end of 2019

2855
02:12:58.410 --> 02:13:00.300
when you came out with this.

2856
02:13:00.300 --> 02:13:01.880
And on a personal level,

2857
02:13:01.880 --> 02:13:04.030
you can't be a phoenix without the fire,

2858
02:13:04.030 --> 02:13:05.940
you gotta burn, right?

2859
02:13:05.940 --> 02:13:10.940
And on a broader level in terms of running in general,

2860
02:13:13.620 --> 02:13:14.943
what an incredible opportunity

2861
02:13:14.943 --> 02:13:19.770
because you're so uniquely situated with your experience,

2862
02:13:19.770 --> 02:13:24.150
and the level of exposure that this story has garnered,

2863
02:13:24.150 --> 02:13:27.660
that you're now perfectly situated

2864
02:13:27.660 --> 02:13:30.760
to reimagine what the future of running can look like

2865
02:13:30.760 --> 02:13:32.910
for girls and women going forward.

2866
02:13:32.910 --> 02:13:35.520
And you've taken that, you're running with it.

2867
02:13:35.520 --> 02:13:37.530
You've got the Tracksmith partnership.

2868
02:13:37.530 --> 02:13:41.290
You've got Atalanta, I said it correctly,

2869
02:13:41.290 --> 02:13:44.350
that's all happening, and it's really inspiring.

2870
02:13:44.350 --> 02:13:46.320
And this has all happened

2871
02:13:46.320 --> 02:13:48.100
in a pretty compressed period of time.

2872
02:13:48.100 --> 02:13:51.700
I mean, I know maybe it seems like not to you,

2873
02:13:51.700 --> 02:13:52.920
but it sounds like it to me,

2874
02:13:52.920 --> 02:13:55.300
like in the grand scheme of things, and you're so young,

2875
02:13:55.300 --> 02:13:57.670
and you have so much running ahead of you,

2876
02:13:57.670 --> 02:13:59.930
and you have so much mentorship ahead of you,

2877
02:13:59.930 --> 02:14:01.530
it's truly inspiring.

2878
02:14:01.530 --> 02:14:04.030
No, and I really appreciate you saying that.

2879
02:14:04.030 --> 02:14:07.760
As I said this probably six weeks between the USADA report

2880
02:14:07.760 --> 02:14:09.870
and when "The New York Times" piece came out,

2881
02:14:09.870 --> 02:14:13.310
felt like the longest six weeks of my life.

2882
02:14:13.310 --> 02:14:17.757
And I think, I always remember that when ever I feel like,

2883
02:14:17.757 --> 02:14:21.030
"Oh gosh, things aren't happening quick enough,"

2884
02:14:21.030 --> 02:14:23.010
or, "I wanna be here by X date,"

2885
02:14:23.010 --> 02:14:26.280
and almost I think,

2886
02:14:26.280 --> 02:14:30.300
or at least my predisposition to push, push, push.

2887
02:14:30.300 --> 02:14:31.133
I always looked back and I'm like,

2888
02:14:31.133 --> 02:14:33.060
"That was only six weeks."

2889
02:14:33.060 --> 02:14:35.260
And so, in the scheme of things,

2890
02:14:35.260 --> 02:14:38.370
it has been a really, really short time,

2891
02:14:38.370 --> 02:14:42.230
which is also why I'm continuing to try to learn.

2892
02:14:42.230 --> 02:14:43.760
I think one thing

2893
02:14:43.760 --> 02:14:46.770
that I do sometimes feel a little uncomfortable with

2894
02:14:46.770 --> 02:14:51.260
is that, we're all flawed individuals, right?

2895
02:14:51.260 --> 02:14:54.650
And so, even me kind of taking this step as a mentor,

2896
02:14:54.650 --> 02:14:55.973
and as an advocate,

2897
02:14:56.940 --> 02:14:59.950
I have to always be very conscious

2898
02:14:59.950 --> 02:15:01.830
of my own place in the world,

2899
02:15:01.830 --> 02:15:04.390
and how I can be educating myself,

2900
02:15:04.390 --> 02:15:07.943
and learning new things, and kind of taking that next step.

2901
02:15:08.880 --> 02:15:12.450
Because for as much as I lived my experience,

2902
02:15:12.450 --> 02:15:17.390
there's so many other moments people can go through

2903
02:15:17.390 --> 02:15:20.143
that I will never experienced and I will never know.

2904
02:15:21.120 --> 02:15:24.037
And to take that level of learning

2905
02:15:24.037 --> 02:15:28.170
and kind of spread this in a way that's more inclusive,

2906
02:15:28.170 --> 02:15:30.170
and not just my story

2907
02:15:31.070 --> 02:15:35.970
can only happen if I'm constantly trying to better myself,

2908
02:15:35.970 --> 02:15:38.610
which is why even with this program that I'm creating

2909
02:15:38.610 --> 02:15:40.900
and the service side of it,

2910
02:15:40.900 --> 02:15:45.330
we're gonna create extensive educational standards

2911
02:15:45.330 --> 02:15:46.483
for all the mentors.

2912
02:15:47.320 --> 02:15:51.080
Because you can't just expect a young,

2913
02:15:51.080 --> 02:15:53.550
well, somebody of any age

2914
02:15:53.550 --> 02:15:56.860
to be ready to kind of teach, right?

2915
02:15:56.860 --> 02:15:58.990
You have to learn before you can teach.

2916
02:15:58.990 --> 02:16:00.040
Right.

2917
02:16:00.040 --> 02:16:02.250
I think you're gonna be really successful with this

2918
02:16:02.250 --> 02:16:05.630
because based on what you just said,

2919
02:16:05.630 --> 02:16:10.630
there's a real appreciation for humility,

2920
02:16:11.890 --> 02:16:14.893
and the level of empathy that you're able to bring to it,

2921
02:16:14.893 --> 02:16:18.870
it just feels, it's such a heart-centered thing for you,

2922
02:16:18.870 --> 02:16:21.690
and I could tell that you've thought it completely through.

2923
02:16:21.690 --> 02:16:24.430
So I'm excited to see what it looks like.

2924
02:16:24.430 --> 02:16:25.850
Yeah. Thank you.

2925
02:16:25.850 --> 02:16:27.180
I can't wait for this journey,

2926
02:16:27.180 --> 02:16:30.810
and I know everything's gonna keep going quick,

2927
02:16:30.810 --> 02:16:33.230
and feeling like it's taking forever,

2928
02:16:33.230 --> 02:16:35.160
but the more that I can stay in the present

2929
02:16:35.160 --> 02:16:36.733
and enjoying that moment,

2930
02:16:37.800 --> 02:16:40.990
I'd always be proud of where I am today,

2931
02:16:40.990 --> 02:16:44.683
as much as proud of what I hope to longterm accomplish.

2932
02:16:45.816 --> 02:16:48.080
I think that's one thing that I'm really working on.

2933
02:16:48.080 --> 02:16:50.990
And I also will kind of share it to anybody else

2934
02:16:50.990 --> 02:16:53.580
who's maybe diving into their next steps,

2935
02:16:53.580 --> 02:16:58.580
or a big endeavor for them is to appreciate the day to day

2936
02:16:58.610 --> 02:17:00.937
and be proud of those little moments,

2937
02:17:00.937 --> 02:17:03.980
and those little steps in the right direction

2938
02:17:03.980 --> 02:17:07.530
because it does go quick when you look back at least,

2939
02:17:07.530 --> 02:17:08.800
even if not in the moment.

2940
02:17:08.800 --> 02:17:09.793
Yeah.

2941
02:17:10.740 --> 02:17:12.480
We got to wrap this up in a couple of minutes,

2942
02:17:12.480 --> 02:17:14.640
but there's a couple more things I wanna touch on

2943
02:17:14.640 --> 02:17:16.593
before I release you to your life.

2944
02:17:17.680 --> 02:17:21.140
I think another reason why the video really worked

2945
02:17:21.140 --> 02:17:24.650
was that it wasn't just you telling your story.

2946
02:17:24.650 --> 02:17:27.650
You were like, "This this is what happened to me,

2947
02:17:27.650 --> 02:17:30.810
but what you need to understand is that

2948
02:17:30.810 --> 02:17:33.330
there's a systemic problem and that needs to change.

2949
02:17:33.330 --> 02:17:34.410
Nike needs to change.

2950
02:17:34.410 --> 02:17:36.580
Nike is too powerful."

2951
02:17:36.580 --> 02:17:39.870
And the investigation that had been launched

2952
02:17:39.870 --> 02:17:44.100
really had nothing to do with the way that you were treated

2953
02:17:44.100 --> 02:17:45.920
or this kind of toxic culture.

2954
02:17:45.920 --> 02:17:48.180
It was all about the doping thing, right?

2955
02:17:48.180 --> 02:17:51.490
And Nike ultimately is going to do what Nike needs to do

2956
02:17:51.490 --> 02:17:53.100
to protect its brand.

2957
02:17:53.100 --> 02:17:58.100
So it's going to basically give lip service to this,

2958
02:17:59.460 --> 02:18:02.730
sweep under the rug, whatever they can get away with,

2959
02:18:02.730 --> 02:18:04.070
and move on.

2960
02:18:04.070 --> 02:18:07.160
And you were the one at the outset calling for

2961
02:18:07.160 --> 02:18:09.590
a third party to conduct this investigation,

2962
02:18:09.590 --> 02:18:12.140
Okay, so they're gonna self police themselves here?

2963
02:18:13.380 --> 02:18:14.860
What does that actually mean?

2964
02:18:14.860 --> 02:18:16.830
Obviously, nothing's gonna happen.

2965
02:18:16.830 --> 02:18:20.010
So, my sense is that that didn't happen.

2966
02:18:20.010 --> 02:18:22.310
There is no third party investigating.

2967
02:18:22.310 --> 02:18:23.400
Is there any update?

2968
02:18:23.400 --> 02:18:24.233
I just wanted to know

2969
02:18:24.233 --> 02:18:29.233
what is the 2021 status update on what's happened there?

2970
02:18:29.830 --> 02:18:34.530
So I think first off there was an internal investigation,

2971
02:18:34.530 --> 02:18:39.530
and I only know this because one reporter was told that.

2972
02:18:39.650 --> 02:18:42.260
And I was reached out for comment

2973
02:18:42.260 --> 02:18:46.540
because I guess there was nothing released besides-

2974
02:18:46.540 --> 02:18:47.373
Nothing public,

2975
02:18:47.373 --> 02:18:49.297
there wasn't a public dossier or something,

2976
02:18:49.297 --> 02:18:50.170
"Here's what happened."

2977
02:18:50.170 --> 02:18:53.870
The only thing that was shared with this journalist,

2978
02:18:53.870 --> 02:18:56.370
Aaron Strout, from "Women's Running,"

2979
02:18:56.370 --> 02:18:59.910
was that they were gonna maybe

2980
02:18:59.910 --> 02:19:04.910
invest more in women and stuff like that, right?

2981
02:19:09.710 --> 02:19:12.423
Super vague, I can't even remember what it was.

2982
02:19:13.940 --> 02:19:17.650
And at the time I remember being asked for comment,

2983
02:19:17.650 --> 02:19:18.483
and I was like,

2984
02:19:18.483 --> 02:19:21.790
"Hey, any time any movement

2985
02:19:21.790 --> 02:19:25.370
is going towards empowering women, that's great."

2986
02:19:25.370 --> 02:19:27.460
Sure, and it's tricky and complicated

2987
02:19:27.460 --> 02:19:28.998
because you look at Serena Williams

2988
02:19:28.998 --> 02:19:31.230
and what they've done with her,

2989
02:19:31.230 --> 02:19:33.010
and it's unbelievable, right?

2990
02:19:33.010 --> 02:19:35.147
So it makes it, it's like, "Okay,"

2991
02:19:35.147 --> 02:19:38.120
and then you tell your story and I don't know what to think.

2992
02:19:38.120 --> 02:19:41.540
Yes, well, I think part of it is that we also have no idea

2993
02:19:41.540 --> 02:19:43.660
behind closed doors what was happening for anybody.

2994
02:19:43.660 --> 02:19:46.761
And it's a company made up of people, right?

2995
02:19:46.761 --> 02:19:48.210
And those individuals turn over.

2996
02:19:48.210 --> 02:19:50.860
People tried to protest within Nike.

2997
02:19:50.860 --> 02:19:52.900
There were like 100 people that protested right after-

2998
02:19:52.900 --> 02:19:55.230
Yeah, and people were threatened to be fired

2999
02:19:55.230 --> 02:19:57.790
if they walked near the Alberto Salazar building,

3000
02:19:57.790 --> 02:19:59.143
that's kind of scary.

3001
02:20:00.000 --> 02:20:02.220
Is it still called The Alberto Salazar building?

3002
02:20:02.220 --> 02:20:03.800
Yep.

3003
02:20:03.800 --> 02:20:07.010
The new Hayward Field, there's a Memorial to him.

3004
02:20:07.010 --> 02:20:09.410
There's a big picture at a stadium

3005
02:20:09.410 --> 02:20:11.040
that I'll probably have to run it multiple times

3006
02:20:11.040 --> 02:20:13.260
over the course of my career.

3007
02:20:13.260 --> 02:20:14.093
Oh my God, yeah.

3008
02:20:14.093 --> 02:20:15.910
And that was built after,

3009
02:20:15.910 --> 02:20:19.770
it was only recently finished, a couple months ago.

3010
02:20:19.770 --> 02:20:21.310
That's right, they just redid it.

3011
02:20:21.310 --> 02:20:22.350
And then they did a reboot.

3012
02:20:22.350 --> 02:20:25.020
So, I think for me, it's one of those things where,

3013
02:20:25.020 --> 02:20:27.430
as you know, you've seen him through the documentation

3014
02:20:27.430 --> 02:20:28.530
I've sent you for this

3015
02:20:28.530 --> 02:20:31.063
my own business that I'm trying to start.

3016
02:20:32.570 --> 02:20:34.950
I don't like using buzzwords,

3017
02:20:34.950 --> 02:20:36.960
and I try to avoid it at all costs.

3018
02:20:36.960 --> 02:20:38.747
So if I say like,

3019
02:20:38.747 --> 02:20:41.890
"I'm trying to empower women,"

3020
02:20:41.890 --> 02:20:44.200
that means nothing to me, right?

3021
02:20:44.200 --> 02:20:45.760
This is actually what I'm gonna do,

3022
02:20:45.760 --> 02:20:48.430
and I'm gonna outlay steps, A, B, C,

3023
02:20:48.430 --> 02:20:49.310
where we're gonna go,

3024
02:20:49.310 --> 02:20:50.810
how we're gonna support it.

3025
02:20:50.810 --> 02:20:52.760
And you know what, if I don't have an answer yet,

3026
02:20:52.760 --> 02:20:54.220
that's always okay.

3027
02:20:54.220 --> 02:20:56.730
But then say, I'm gonna have to lean on these partners,

3028
02:20:56.730 --> 02:20:58.980
and these experts, and take these next steps.

3029
02:21:00.060 --> 02:21:05.060
And so, I think the big maybe takeaways

3030
02:21:05.120 --> 02:21:09.010
if you're a multi-billion dollar organization,

3031
02:21:09.010 --> 02:21:11.810
is actually care,

3032
02:21:11.810 --> 02:21:13.117
and actually figure out like,

3033
02:21:13.117 --> 02:21:16.010
"Okay, if we're gonna do something, what are we gonna do?

3034
02:21:16.010 --> 02:21:17.240
And how are we gonna do it?"

3035
02:21:17.240 --> 02:21:21.750
And don't just keep coming out with ads that

3036
02:21:21.750 --> 02:21:23.480
even recently support

3037
02:21:25.080 --> 02:21:29.260
women who are pregnant and are athletes, right?

3038
02:21:29.260 --> 02:21:31.010
'Cause I watched that, and I think,

3039
02:21:32.267 --> 02:21:35.700
"You've never acknowledged how you treated Kara,

3040
02:21:35.700 --> 02:21:37.230
Alicea, Alison,"

3041
02:21:37.230 --> 02:21:39.627
there's never been any sort of like,

3042
02:21:39.627 --> 02:21:42.230
"Hey, we did wrong."

3043
02:21:42.230 --> 02:21:44.990
And I think I have always felt that

3044
02:21:44.990 --> 02:21:48.280
leaders are not people who do everything right.

3045
02:21:48.280 --> 02:21:49.140
Leaders are people

3046
02:21:49.140 --> 02:21:51.540
who are always trying to better themselves.

3047
02:21:51.540 --> 02:21:54.120
Always know they have places to learn,

3048
02:21:54.120 --> 02:21:57.240
and can acknowledge that they're going to fail some times.

3049
02:21:57.240 --> 02:22:01.747
And in those moments can step up and say,

3050
02:22:01.747 --> 02:22:02.740
"I'm sorry,

3051
02:22:02.740 --> 02:22:06.560
and this is how I'm going to change going forward."

3052
02:22:06.560 --> 02:22:08.510
Sure. They take responsibility.

3053
02:22:08.510 --> 02:22:13.510
I see it as, look you can try to whitewash this,

3054
02:22:13.560 --> 02:22:15.470
and put out a bunch of marketing campaigns,

3055
02:22:15.470 --> 02:22:17.190
and the truth is

3056
02:22:17.190 --> 02:22:19.340
the average public isn't paying attention to this.

3057
02:22:19.340 --> 02:22:21.362
No, of course, yeah.
So, it's not, is it?

3058
02:22:21.362 --> 02:22:24.420
So, how concerned are they really?

3059
02:22:24.420 --> 02:22:26.670
But ultimately, it seems to me

3060
02:22:26.670 --> 02:22:29.670
in their long-term growth interest

3061
02:22:29.670 --> 02:22:31.550
to really reckon with this,

3062
02:22:31.550 --> 02:22:35.521
the amount of goodwill that they would be able to engender

3063
02:22:35.521 --> 02:22:39.540
if the new CEO said, "I'm getting to the bottom of this.

3064
02:22:39.540 --> 02:22:42.220
I'm taking it super seriously,"

3065
02:22:42.220 --> 02:22:45.880
